<font size=3><b>Techs slump with Intel</b></font><br>
With investors selling Intel shares before its post-market close earnings announcement, technology stocks dropped Tuesday.
<p>
Despite generally upbeat remarks on the economy by Fed Chair Alan Greenspan and news of a profitable quarter from Nextel Communications, CNET's Tech index slipped 12.4 points, or 1.25 percent, to 992.91. The tech-laden Nasdaq composite index fell 7.36 points, or 0.53 percent, to 1,375.26.
<p>
Worse-than-expected earnings from construction machinery maker Caterpillar helped depress broader markets. The Dow Jones industrial average lost 166.0 points, or 1.92 percent, to 8,473.1--for its seventh consecutive losing session. The S&P 500 shed 16.99 points, or 1.85 percent, to 900.94--another multi-year low.
<br><br>
</font></td>
<td width=8><img src=""http://www.cnet.com/b.gif"" width=8 height=1></td></tr>
