</table>

<font size=""+1""><b>Rack server a la mode</b></a></font><br>

With its Xserve rack-mount server, <b>Apple is moving into enterprise territory</b>. The specs are impressive: Dual 1GHz 
PowerPC G4s, up to 2GB DDR SDRAM, two 64-bit 66MHz PCI slots (plus a third combination PCI/AGP slot), dual Gigabit Ethernet, 
FireWire and USB ports, and four Ultra ATA/100 Apple Drive Module bays. But <b>Bill O'Brien</b> thinks Apple's 
<b>licensing</b> may be even more appealing than the hardware.

<br><img src=""http://www.zdnet.com/techupdate/i/arrow_blue.gif"" width=""8"" height=""10"" border=""0"">
<a href=""http://clickthru.online.com/Click?q=12-jaAKIl-XYrs-Xbl-pEvKY-qkCKnR"" >
<b>Read the full story</b></a>


<p>



